WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.594
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:15.031
Unit four: Free Time Activities. Today you will talk about what you like and enjoy doing.

4
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:18.215
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.446
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:24.284
Leisure.

7
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:28.351
Leisure means free time when you are not working or studying.

8
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.217
In my leisure time, I read comics.

9
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.074
Your turn. Say: Leisure.

10
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:37.934
Leisure.

11
00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:39.661
Board game.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.927
Board game means a game played on a board with pieces.

13
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:46.934
We play board games on rainy days.

14
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.924
Your turn. Say: Board game.

15
00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:53.872
Board game.

16
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:55.536
Sketch.

17
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.933
Sketch means to draw something quickly.

18
00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:01.307
I like to sketch people in the park.

19
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:04.511
Your turn. Say: Sketch.

20
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.228
Sketch.

21
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:09.775
Collect.

22
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:13.723
Collect means to get and keep things of the same kind.

23
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:16.038
My brother collects stamps.

24
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.942
Your turn. Say: Collect.

25
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.731
Collect.

26
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.461
Podcast.

27
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.796
Podcast means a recorded talk show you can listen to online.

28
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.638
I listen to an English podcast.

29
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.972
Your turn. Say: Podcast.

30
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:38.869
Podcast.

31
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:40.792
Skateboard.

32
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:44.538
Skateboard means to ride on a board with wheels.

33
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.999
We skateboard at Koh Pich.

34
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:50.398
Your turn. Say: Skateboard.

35
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:54.339
Skateboard.

36
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.212
Karaoke.

37
00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:00.273
Karaoke means singing to music with words on a screen.

38
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:03.243
My family loves karaoke at parties.

39
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.560
Your turn. Say: Karaoke.

40
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.517
Karaoke.

41
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:12.308
Relax.

42
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.885
Relax means to rest and feel calm.

43
00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:18.587
I relax by listening to music.

44
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:21.522
Your turn. Say: Relax.

45
00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.484
Relax.

46
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:26.961
Bore.

47
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.565
Bore means to make someone feel not interested.

48
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.766
Long films bore me.

49
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.642
Your turn. Say: Bore.

50
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.327
Bore.

51
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:41.131
Entertain.

52
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:44.975
Entertain means to make people enjoy themselves.

53
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:47.699
Magic shows entertain children.

54
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:51.319
Your turn. Say: Entertain.

55
00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:55.145
Entertain.

56
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:56.966
Pastime.

57
00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.588
Pastime means an activity you do for fun.

58
00:03:01.183 --> 00:03:03.694
Fishing is my uncle's favorite pastime.

59
00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.703
Your turn. Say: Pastime.

60
00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.603
Pastime.

61
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:12.456
Spend time.

62
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.053
Spend time means to use your time doing something.

63
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.160
I spend time with my friends after school.

64
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.275
Your turn. Say: Spend time.

65
00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.134
Spend time.

66
00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:30.654
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:34.329
Visal, what do you enjoy doing in your leisure time?

68
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:38.461
I enjoy skateboarding with my friends.

69
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.724
Do you like listening to podcasts?

70
00:03:42.817 --> 00:03:47.605
Yes, I like listening to English podcasts. They help me learn.

71
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:49.880
And what bores you?

72
00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:54.135
Waiting bores me! I don't like doing nothing.

73
00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.649
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:57.483 --> 00:04:00.806
Grammar focus: like and enjoy plus verb-ing.

75
00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.270
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:02.983 --> 00:04:04.402
I enjoy sketching.

77
00:04:05.317 --> 00:04:07.363
I like listening to podcasts.

78
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.366
She enjoys playing board games.

79
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.947
After 'enjoy', always use verb-ing: I enjoy reading — not I enjoy to read.

80
00:04:16.683 --> 00:04:20.044
Be careful! Don't say: I enjoy to sketch.

81
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.570
Say: I enjoy sketching.

82
00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.079
After 'enjoy', use the -ing form.

83
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:29.565
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.588
My Leisure Time.

85
00:04:31.888 --> 00:04:36.245
In my leisure time, I enjoy sketching and listening to podcasts.

86
00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:40.185
My favorite pastime on weekends is skateboarding.

87
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.606
My sister likes collecting stickers.

88
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.062
On Saturday nights, our family enjoys singing karaoke.

89
00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.844
Spending time with people I love helps me relax.

90
00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:56.773
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:57.617 --> 00:04:59.558
I enjoy blank board games.

92
00:04:59.858 --> 00:05:03.279
A, playing. B, play. C, to play.

93
00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:08.694
The answer is A: playing.

94
00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.850
To draw something quickly is to blank.

95
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:16.453
A, sketch. B, collect. C, relax.

96
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.046
The answer is A: sketch.

97
00:05:23.183 --> 00:05:25.752
An activity you do for fun is a blank.

98
00:05:26.052 --> 00:05:30.239
A, pastime. B, podcast. C, leisure.

99
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.043
The answer is A: pastime.

100
00:05:37.233 --> 00:05:40.246
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:43.826
What do you usually do to relax after school?

102
00:05:52.617 --> 00:05:54.071
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:54.371 --> 00:06:01.388
After school, I enjoy listening to music and sketching. On weekends, I like skateboarding with my friends.

104
00:06:01.688 --> 00:06:03.328
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:04.217 --> 00:06:09.226
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and like and enjoy plus verb-ing.

106
00:06:09.526 --> 00:06:13.734
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

107
00:06:14.034 --> 00:06:16.582
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

108
00:06:16.882 --> 00:06:19.488
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

